    <item>
      <title>You can negotiate everything</title>
      <link>/bookstack/you_can_negotiate_everything/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/bookstack/you_can_negotiate_everything/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;TOC&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#what-is-negotiation&#34;&gt;What is negotiation?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#about-the-three-elements-of-a-negotitation&#34;&gt;About the three elements of a negotitation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#power&#34;&gt;Power&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#time&#34;&gt;Time&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#information&#34;&gt;Information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#styles-of-negotiation&#34;&gt;Styles of negotiation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#the-soviet-style-win-lose&#34;&gt;The soviet style (Win-Lose)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#negotiation-for-mutual-satisfaction-win-win&#34;&gt;Negotiation for mutual satisfaction (Win-Win)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#more-on-the-win-win-technique&#34;&gt;More on the Win-Win technique&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#has-it-worked-my-final-evaluation&#34;&gt;Has it worked? My final evaluation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The first time you come across &lt;em&gt;You can negotiate everything&lt;/em&gt; by Herb Cohen it can appears one of those books full of techniques to manipulate people and persuade them to do what you want. But if you move beyond this first impression you can find a useful book written by someone who certainly was effective in the pragmatic art of getting someone to agree with you, but was also persuaded that the best way to do this was to build a good relationship based on trust with the other side in every negotiation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
